# AOB Speakeasy — fork-owned files, protected from the daily upstream merge.
#
# These files exist upstream too, but ours are deliberately different: upstream's versions
# advertise MiroTalk, carry its sponsorship and affiliate links, and route bug and conduct
# reports to its maintainer. Without this, every upstream edit to them would either
# conflict (failing the sync job) or quietly reintroduce that content here.
#
# `merge=ours` keeps OUR version whenever both sides changed the file. It requires the
# driver to be defined; the sync workflow does that with:
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# If you merge upstream by hand on a local clone, run that once there as well — otherwise
# git falls back to a normal merge and you will get conflicts in these files.
#
# Trade-off, stated plainly: genuine upstream improvements to these four files are
# discarded along with the marketing. In practice upstream only edits them to rotate
# sponsors, so the trade is worth it — but it is a trade.

README.md            merge=ours
SECURITY.md          merge=ours
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md   merge=ours
.github/FUNDING.yml  merge=ours
.gitattributes       merge=ours
